          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em tower
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            of the shape of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\cdots \to X_2 \to X_1 \to X_0
                  \\,.
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
            over a diagram of this form is called a
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+limit"} sequential limit
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+limit"} directed limit
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{i+1}\to X_i
            are epimorphism then we sometimes say that the tower is a
            %span.newWikiWord
              cofiltration
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/cofiltration"} ?
            (though the same term may be sometimes applied more generally for more general index categories, or more restrictively when there is an object in the ambient category such that all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_i
            are its quotients).
          %p
            Different contexts lead to different notions of morphism of towers, so it is important to consider what category of towers is appropriate for any given use of these objects. In addition to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Postnikov+towers"} Postnikov towers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pro-object"} pro-object
            in a category. In that situation the morphisms considered between towers are usually pro-morphisms.
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            in the presence of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-limits"} (infinity,1)-limits
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-colimits"} (infinity,1)-colimits
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tower+of+homotopy+fibers"} tower of homotopy fibers
          %h2#TheProCategoryOfTowers The pro-category of towers
          %h3#definition Definition
          %p
            The tower diagram shape
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mo ≥
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mn 3
                  %mo →
                  %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}_{\geq} = \{\cdots 3\to 2 \to 1 \to 0\}
            is evidently a small
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofiltered+category"} cofiltered category
            %em pro-morphisms
            between tower diagrams:
          #ProCategoryOfTowers.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              For any small category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Tow
                      %mi pro
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mrow
                    %mi Pro
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    i
                    \\;\colon\;
                    Tow_{pro}(\mathcal{C})
                    \\overset{}{\hookrightarrow}
                    Pro(\mathcal{C})
                    \\hookrightarrow
                    PSh(\mathcal{C})
            %p
              of the category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Pro
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Pro(\mathcal{C})
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pro-objects"} pro-objects
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              on those that have presentation by formal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+limits"} sequential limits
              (formal limits over tower diagrams) is the
              %strong pro-category of towers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Tow
                      %mi pro
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tow_{pro}(\mathcal{C})
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Blanc96"} Blanc 96, def. 2.5
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mo ≥
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet \colon \mathbb{N}_{\geq} \longrightarrow \mathcal{C}
            a tower diagram, we write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo ⟵
                    %mi f
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mo •
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi Tow
                    %mi pro
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Pro
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\underset{\longleftarrow}{\lim}^f X_\bullet \in Tow_{pro}(\mathcal{C}) \hookrightarrow Pro(\mathcal{C})
          %p for its formal cofiltered limit, i.e.
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo ⟵
                    %mi f
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Tow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msub
                    %mi Top
                    %mi pro
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\underset{\longleftarrow}{\lim}^f
                  \\;\colon\;
                  Tow(\mathcal{C})
                  \\longrightarrow
                  Top_{pro}(\mathcal{C})
                  \\,.
          %h3#properties Properties
          %p
            Notice that generally we have that morphisms between formal cofiltered limits (pro-objects) of shapes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒦
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{K}_1
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒦
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{K}_2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒦
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{K}
            equipped with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/final+functors"} final functors
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒦
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{K}_1
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒦
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{K}_2
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ind-object"} ind-object
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "ind-object#MorphismsRepresentedByCofilteredSystemsOfMorphisms"} this prop.
          %p
            The following says that in the case that both shapes are towers, then also
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒦
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{K}
            may always be chosen to be of tower shape:
          #ProMorphismsBetweenTowerDiagrams.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y_\bullet
              two tower diagrams in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %munder
                        %mi lim
                        %mo ⟵
                      %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %munder
                        %mi lim
                        %mo ⟵
                      %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\phi
                    \\;\colon\;
                    \\underset{\longleftarrow}{\lim}^f X_\bullet
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\underset{\longleftarrow}{\lim}^f Y_\bullet
            %p
              between their formal cofiltered limits (every pro-morphism between the diagrams) in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Tow
                      %mi pro
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Pro
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tow_{pro}(\mathcal{C}) \hookrightarrow Pro(\mathcal{C})
              is represented by component morphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi k
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi h
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\phi_{k} \;\colon\; X_{h(k)} \longrightarrow Y_k
            %p
              making
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagrams"} commuting diagrams
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mrow
                                %mi h
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi k
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi ϕ
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi k
                                    %mo +
                                    %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Y
                              %mrow
                                %mi k
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mrow
                                %mi h
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi k
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi ϕ
                                  %mi k
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Y
                              %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X_{h(k+1)} &amp;\overset{\phi_{k+1}}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y_{k+1}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow
                    \\\
                    X_{h(k)}
                    \&amp;\underset{\phi_k}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    Y_k
                    }
            %p
              i.e. by a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_\bullet
              between
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mo ≥
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi h
                    %msub
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mo ≥
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mo •
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{N}_{\geq} \overset{h}{\longrightarrow} \mathbb{N}_{\geq} \overset{X_\bullet}{\longrightarrow} \mathcal{C}
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mo ≥
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Y
                          %mo •
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{N}_{\geq} \overset{Y_\bullet}{\longrightarrow} \mathcal{C}
            %p as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %munder
                        %mi lim
                        %mo ⟵
                      %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\phi \simeq \underset{\longleftarrow}{\lim}^f (\phi_\bullet)
                    \\,.
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Blanc96"} Blanc 96, p. 6
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Libman"} Libman, p.4
          #FiniteLimitsInProCategoryOfTowers.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              The pro-category of towers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Tow
                      %mi pro
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tow_{pro}(\mathcal{C})
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProCategoryOfTowers"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits"} finite limits
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+colimits"} finite colimits
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProMorphismsBetweenTowerDiagrams"}
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Blanc96"}> Blanc 96, pop. 2.7
            )
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Postnikov+tower"} Postnikov tower
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead+tower"} Whitehead tower
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chromatic+tower"} chromatic tower
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+object+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} filtered object in an (infinity,1)-category
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li#Blanc96
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Blanc"}> David Blanc
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Colimits for the pro-category of towers of simplicial sets
                = succeed ")" do
